WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.684
In this lesson, you will learn to Snap a
window without dragging it,

00:00:05.684 --> 00:00:06.876
using the Zone picker.

00:00:07.226 --> 00:00:08.080
On a trackpad,

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.291
holding a key while you drag a window
across the screen is hard work.

00:00:12.291 --> 00:00:14.244
The Zone picker needs one click.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.354
Every standard window has three buttons at
its top left corner.

00:00:19.354 --> 00:00:21.311
The green one is the one we need.

00:00:21.681 --> 00:00:26.220
Hold Command, and rest the pointer on the
green button. Keep it still for a moment.

00:00:26.578 --> 00:00:28.987
The Zone picker opens under the button.

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.644
It is a small copy of the display's
Layout,

00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:34.238
with the same Zone numbers as the overlay.

00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:37.606
You can let go of Command now. The picker
stays open.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:38.899
Point at a Zone.

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:43.150
Watch the screen: Zonal shows where the
window will land before you click.

00:00:43.531 --> 00:00:45.677
Click the Zone, and the window Snaps
there.

00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:50.819
To close the picker without Snapping, move
the pointer away, or press Escape.

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:51.667
Nothing moves.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.978
Without Command, the green button works as
usual,

00:00:54.978 --> 00:00:57.377
so the Zone picker never gets in your way.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.970
When is the green button the best choice?

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.588
On a laptop trackpad.

00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:06.515
Instead of holding a key during a long
drag, you point and click.

00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:09.663
For a window that is far from where it
belongs,

00:01:09.663 --> 00:01:12.343
like one at the other end of a large
display.

00:01:12.343 --> 00:01:13.892
One click, and it is home.

00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:18.573
It can span too: Control-click several
Zones in the picker to select them,

00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:21.617
then click once more to Snap the window
across them.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:27.237
To recap. Hold Command and rest the
pointer on the green button.

00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:30.353
Point at a Zone to preview it, and click
to Snap.

00:01:30.353 --> 00:01:32.707
Move away, or press Escape, to close.

00:01:34.257 --> 00:01:37.391
In the next lesson, you will learn to Snap
with the keyboard,

00:01:37.391 --> 00:01:39.139
without touching the mouse at all.
